From 59613c3b736c889c396173a917fc2bd4995cfd82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpkt9762 <cpkt9762@163.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:49:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): local sync administration for the Paseo adapter

Add the loopback-only HTTP surface the Paseo plugin needs to manage cloud
sync from the desktop app, without touching the memory protocol contract
(none of these routes is bound to an operation or listed as a supporting
route, so the Pi and DSH runtime-contract projections stay identical):

- GET /health advertises sync-admin-v1 and sync-admin-v2.
- GET and POST and DELETE /sync/enrollment read, join and stop cloud sync
  for a project. POST and DELETE go through requireAuth plus loopback Host,
  no-Origin and JSON checks and are bound to the instance id.
- GET /prompts/secret-scan pages through a project's prompts and returns
  masked matches with a scan token. POST /sync/enrollment recomputes the
  token in the enrollment transaction and answers 409 scan_stale when new
  prompts arrived; force skips that check on purpose.
- GET /prompts/recent and /prompts/search accept masked=1. The display mask
  replaces the whole detected value, including short ones, and also covers
  Chinese keywords followed by ASCII values and standalone replies after a
  credential question. Stored text and the persistence redaction are
  unchanged.
- DELETE /prompts/{id} and DELETE /observations/{id} take optional
  instance_id, and prompts take expected_project, checked in the delete
  transaction.
- GET /sync/status adds target, pending_count, last_success_at, status_at,
  paused, cloud_configured, autosync_enabled, enrolled_count and
  blocked_projects. A project the cloud rejects with project_not_allowed is
  reported until the next completed attempt or unenrollment. Without a
  status provider the old message field is kept, and a cloud configuration
  error is reported in the body instead of failing the endpoint.

Stopping sync only deletes the enrollment row: pending uploads stay queued
but are not uploaded, inbound pulls continue, rows written meanwhile are
backfilled on re-enrollment, and edits to already acked rows are not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
